./contributingGuides/STYLE.md:990:In React Native, one **must not** attempt to falsey-check a string for an inline ternary. Even if it's in curly braces, React Native will try to render it as a `<Text>` node and most likely throw an error about trying to render text outside of a `<Text>` component. Use `!!` instead.
